0.12 0.23 0.54 rg BT /F2 12 Tf 50 588 Td (1. Purpose of the Study) Tj ET
0.12 0.16 0.24 rg BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 572 Td (You are participating in a research study investigating human motor performance in rapid aimed target acquisition,) Tj ET
0.12 0.16 0.24 rg BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 558 Td (guided by the mathematical principles of Fitts Law. The objective is to empirically evaluate movement time and) Tj ET
0.12 0.16 0.24 rg BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 544 Td (trajectory precision across diverse amplitudes \(distances\), target widths \(sizes\), and movement directions.) Tj ET
0.12 0.23 0.54 rg BT /F2 12 Tf 50 518 Td (2. Description of Experimental Procedure) Tj ET
0.12 0.16 0.24 rg BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 502 Td (During this session, you will complete 10 testing blocks consisting of 32 distinct target acquisition tasks \(total 320 trials\).) Tj ET
0.12 0.16 0.24 rg BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 488 Td (For each trial, you will reposition your cursor at the center of the screen, click the center start circle, and then swiftly move) Tj ET
0.12 0.16 0.24 rg BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 474 Td (and click on a circular target displayed on either the left or right side of the screen as quickly and accurately as possible.) Tj ET
